  "verbalization": "Zeylanol appears to have a direct relationship with Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta, as it is identified as a target of two distinct entities: ADP-ribosylation factor-like protein 3 and Voltage-dependent T-type calcium channel subunit alpha-1I. Both of these entities are themselves targets of other molecules, with Eucalyptus gum acting as a target of the latter. This suggests that Zeylanol may exert its effects through a series of molecular pathways that ultimately lead to the inhibition or modulation of Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta. The presence of multiple indirect targets implies that Zeylanol may interact with the lipid metabolism pathway, potentially influencing the activity of this enzyme. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible role for Zeylanol in modulating lipid signaling through the action of these downstream targets.",
